(vector (map (:db/id -1), (:adr/id "ADR-2608132810"), (:adr/title "The 41 distributed task runners were 35 repos, none hand-edited: 30 swept, 5 owed"), (:adr/status "accepted"), (:adr/date "2026-08-13"), (:adr/supersedes ""), (:adr/superseded-by ""), (:adr/body "## Context\n\nADR-2608131400 fixed scripts/bb_edn_to_nbb_tasks.cljs, whose generated runner\ndiscarded spawnSync's .error and .signal and returned (or (.-status r) 1). With\nstdio inherited there is no child to write anything, so a task that could not\nstart was byte-for-byte indistinguishable from one that ran and failed quietly:\nexit 1, zero bytes on both streams. That ADR deliberately did NOT sweep the\nalready-distributed copies, reasoning that they were hand-maintained and working.\n\nADR-2608131600 then measured the damage and recorded the sweep as owed. This ADR\nperforms it.\n\n## Distinct repositories versus paths\n\nls orgs/*/*/scripts/run-task.cljs returns 41 checkout paths. Six of them are\nstale pre-rename duplicates resolving, through gh api repos/<org>/<repo> --jq\n.full_name, onto a repo already in the list:\n\n  etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-joucho        -> etzhayyim/actor-joucho\n  etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-shinka        -> etzhayyim/actor-shinka\n  etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-sip           -> kotoba-lang/kami-app-sip\n  gftdcojp/ai-gftd-oshikatsu            -> cloud-itonami/oshikatsu\n  kotoba-lang/murakumo-studio           -> kotoba-lang/cloud-murakumo-studio\n  network-awai/network-isekai-playtest  -> network-awai/network-isekai\n\nThe last one 404s on the API (the old name is gone rather than redirected); its\ncheckout's git remote resolves it: git@github.com:network-awai/network-isekai.\n\n  41 paths, 35 DISTINCT repositories.\n\nThe path count double-counts. Every figure below is de-duplicated.\n\n## How many runners had diverged: zero\n\nThe premise for not sweeping was that the copies had been hand-edited. They had\nnot. Measured two ways:\n\n  1. All 41 working-tree files hash to 4d9df5220808c8309f48cf200c9ba3a5f86abb5e\n     (one sha256, 41 files, 1886 bytes each).\n  2. The same holds on each repo's origin/main -- read from <remote>/main after\n     a fetch, not from the local checkout, because several checkouts are behind\n     their west pins. 41 of 41 hash to that same value.\n\nAnd that value is byte-identical to the run-task-src string literal extracted\nfrom the generator at its pre-fix commit (5d3042b1fda^). So all 41 copies were\npristine generator output; 0 had diverged; the targeted-edit machinery prepared\nfor hand-modified files was never needed, and writing the current template\nverbatim is exactly equal to applying the sh fix in place.\n\nWhat the copies were missing was therefore both changes the generator carries:\nthe sh reporting of .error/.signal, and the replacement of the three\n(binding [*out* *err*] (println ...)) diagnostics that nbb does not honour\n(ADR-2608130600) -- that text was landing on stdout.\n\n## Verification\n\nBoth templates run against the same synthetic registry, so the difference is\nattributable to the runner alone:\n\n  {:missing   {:cmd [\"definitely-not-a-real-binary\" \"--flag\"]}\n   :wholeline {:cmd [\"clojure -M:test\"]}\n   :real      {:cmd [\"echo\" \"HELLO-FROM-TASK\"]}}\n\n  PRE-FIX runner\n    missing    exit=1  stdout=[]                 stderr=[]\n    wholeline  exit=1  stdout=[]                 stderr=[]\n    real       exit=0  stdout=[HELLO-FROM-TASK]  stderr=[]\n\n  FIXED runner\n    missing    exit=1  stderr=[run-task: could not start [\"definitely-not-a-real-binary\" \"--flag\"] -- spawnSync definitely-not-a-real-binary ENOENT]\n    wholeline  exit=1  stderr=[run-task: could not start [\"clojure -M:test\"] -- spawnSync clojure -M:test ENOENT]\n    real       exit=0  stdout=[HELLO-FROM-TASK]  stderr=[]\n\nAgainst real repositories, reading the runner as it now stands on main:\n\n  kotoba-lang/kami-mangaka-render (worktree cut from kotoba-lang/main after the merge)\n    unknown task  exit=2  stdout=[]  stderr=[unknown task: no-such / known: test]\n      -- the diagnostic is on stderr now; before the sweep it printed on stdout\n    test          exit=0  Ran 8 tests containing 37 assertions.\n\n  network-awai/network-isekai (worktree cut from network-awai/main after the merge)\n    lobby-server BEFORE argv split\n      exit=1  stdout=0 bytes\n      stderr=[run-task: could not start [\"node --test\" \"test/isekai/lobby_server_test.mjs\"] -- spawnSync node --test ENOENT]\n    lobby-server AFTER  exit=0, pass 21 / fail 0\n    analytics-e2e AFTER exit=1, now reaching node and failing on its real missing\n                        wrangler/D1 backend (npm ERR! cb.apply is not a function)\n                        rather than on nothing\n\n  cloud-itonami/oshikatsu and gftdcojp/ai-gftd-isekai (archived, see below)\n    test BEFORE  exit=1  stdout=0 bytes\n                 stderr=[run-task: could not start [\"clojure -M:test\"] -- spawnSync clojure -M:test ENOENT]\n    test AFTER the argv split\n      oshikatsu       exit=0  Ran 1 tests containing 4 assertions.\n      ai-gftd-isekai  exit=0  Ran 2 tests containing 6 assertions.\n\n## A second one-element predicate that walked past two live failures\n\nThe census counted registered tasks whose :cmd was a ONE-element vector\ncontaining whitespace. Re-scanning every origin/main tasks.edn for the actual\ndefect -- any :cmd whose FIRST element contains whitespace, whatever the vector's\nlength -- found two more in network-awai/network-isekai:\n\n  lobby-server   [\"node --test\" \"test/isekai/lobby_server_test.mjs\"]\n  analytics-e2e  [\"node --test\" \"test/isekai/analytics_e2e.mjs\"]\n\nBoth are two-element vectors whose first element carries the flag, so the\none-element predicate did not see them, and the 2026-08-13 repair (55e9d39) that\nsplit the other ten in that same file walked straight past these two. This is the\ncensus's own stated defect class -- a classifier that pattern-matches a shape\nnarrower than the defect -- recurring one layer up. Repaired and merged\n(690c3b9e).\n\nAfter that repair the only remaining first-element-with-whitespace :cmd entries\nin the whole fleet are the two in the archived repositories below. The census\nfigure of 23 such tasks across five checkout paths was measured before the\nnetwork-isekai repair landed and before path de-duplication.\n\n## Swept: 30 of 35 distinct repositories\n\nEach: worktree cut explicitly from <remote>/main outside the superproject root,\none commit, push, server-side merge via gh api repos/<full>/merges, then worktree\nand both branches deleted. Verified afterwards by re-reading scripts/run-task.cljs\nfrom each origin/main and hashing it against the fixed template.\n\n  cloud-itonami/actor-kawaraban          098a26e5\n  cloud-itonami/kuni-umi                 d5e200e4\n  cloud-itonami/narashi                  d078d4ea\n  com-junkawasaki/org-spirit-in-physics-comics  d9854b2f\n  etzhayyim/actor-joucho                 2af7d361\n  etzhayyim/actor-shinka                 ceba1398\n  etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-tomoshibi      b5fa89d9\n  kotoba-lang/aiueos                     a36c45a1\n  kotoba-lang/cloud-murakumo-studio      00de3e4d\n  kotoba-lang/freeboard                  4e3d981c\n  kotoba-lang/io-ipfs                    507c950d\n  kotoba-lang/io-multiformats            e7ae323d\n  kotoba-lang/kami-app-sip               bff2d8e8\n  kotoba-lang/kami-engine                c2646df7\n  kotoba-lang/kami-genko                 9030e305\n  kotoba-lang/kami-isekai-assets         0d1635e0\n  kotoba-lang/kami-mangaka-expression    e2205340\n  kotoba-lang/kami-mangaka-page          fc94a6f1\n  kotoba-lang/kami-mangaka-render        27745577\n  kotoba-lang/kisekae                    04ef7a88\n  kotoba-lang/org-chainagnostic-cacao    693edbba\n  kotoba-lang/org-ietf-cbor              2e9a6f8e\n  kotoba-lang/org-ietf-ed25519           d6393e2a\n  kotoba-lang/org-ietf-turn              bdef0bf3\n  kotoba-lang/org-signal                 7f2e9556\n  kotoba-lang/org-w3-webrtc-signaling    987a769e\n  kotoba-lang/webgpu                     7a0ff33f\n  network-awai/cloud-itonami             71d50a97\n  network-awai/local-manimani            2d740c2a\n  network-awai/network-isekai            9192c880 (+ 690c3b9e argv split)\n\n## Not swept: 5 of 35, with reasons\n\nARCHIVED AND READ-ONLY -- 3 repositories. Changes are written, committed on a\nlocal branch agent/run-task-sh-report in each checkout, and verified by\nexecution; they cannot be pushed. Do not unarchive on my initiative.\n\n  cloud-itonami/oshikatsu        runner + tasks.edn argv split (6fbb7bc)\n  gftdcojp/ai-gftd-isekai        runner + tasks.edn argv split (09d3fbb)\n  etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-kuni_umi   runner only (bca403a); empty registry, so\n                                     nothing was silently failing there\n\n  On all three, gh api repos/<full> --jq .permissions.push reads TRUE while\n  .archived reads true. A permissions check does not reveal this. The push does:\n  \"This repository was archived so it is read-only\" (HTTP 403).\n\n  The census named two archived repositories; the third, com-etzhayyim-kuni_umi,\n  carries a stale runner too and is equally owed, even though it lost no task.\n\nkotoba-lang/murakumo -- branch protection. The merges API refused with 409:\n  protected branch 'main' check failed: Required status check \"test\" is expected.\n  GitHub Actions is disabled org-wide (ADR-2607300900), so that check can never\n  report and the merge can never become allowed by waiting. Branch pushed and\n  left as PR kotoba-lang/murakumo#294 for an owner. Forging the status via the\n  commit-status API would satisfy the gate while checking nothing, which is the\n  same failure this ADR is about.\n\netzhayyim/root -- its own pre-commit gate. lefthook runs e7m-verify, a whole-repo\n  constitutional scan, on any commit with staged files. It fails today on an\n  invariant unrelated to this change:\n    transparent_force  FAIL  transparent-force retirement provenance missing\n    8/9 constitutional invariants verified\n  Confirmed pre-existing rather than caused by the change: running\n  PYTHONPATH=70-tools/e7m/src python3 -m e7m --json verify on an UNMODIFIED tree\n  cut from etzhayyim/main returns ok:false. An empty commit passes, because the\n  whole-repo scan only runs when files are staged, so it is not that commits are\n  blocked -- it is that any commit touching a file is. Not bypassed with\n  --no-verify: silently stepping over another repo's constitutional gate to land\n  a one-file change is a worse trade than leaving the change owed. Owed, with the\n  fix being exactly the current run-task-src literal in\n  scripts/bb_edn_to_nbb_tasks.cljs.\n\n## Also not done\n\nThe 129 (a)-class dropped tasks from ADR-2608131600 remain owed; they are ports,\nnot conversions. cloud-itonami/kuni-umi's tasks.edn still shells out to bb and is\na facade rather than a conversion; its runner was swept but its one task still\ninvokes the binary ADR-2607173000 retired. The README drift the census called\nworse than the missing tasks is untouched.\n\n## Note on method\n\nAn early version of this sweep assigned the loop variable name `path` in zsh,\nwhich is tied to the PATH array; the shell lost every external command mid-run\nand, before that, created symlinks from the scratch worktree directory into the\nlive orgs/ tree. No child repository was written through them -- every iteration\nfailed at git worktree add -- but a stray worktree had been created against\nanother session's branch fix/jvm-test-root-causes. The symlinks were removed by\nunlinking (never the targets), the worktree was removed with its branch left\nintact, and the sweep was re-run with non-special variable names. Recorded\nbecause the failure mode is silent and repo-shaped: a clobbered PATH turns a\nloop over shared checkouts into something that can touch them by accident.\n")))
